# Stacking effects, most of them off.
#
# The point of this script is what it does NOT cost. Every stage below is
# available, and a stage that is switched off -- or whose settings would change
# nothing -- is skipped entirely: no allocation, no dispatch, no copy. Its
# output aliases its input, so the pixels flow straight through.
#
# That is what makes a long stack practical. Twenty effects with three in use
# allocates three intermediates, not twenty, and at 45 MP that is the
# difference between a usable pipeline and one that pages.
#
# TWO WAYS TO TURN A STAGE OFF, and they are for different moments:
#
#   enabled        every algorithm has this checkbox, first in its group. Use
#                  it once the sliders are where you want them: it switches the
#                  stage out and leaves every other setting exactly as it was,
#                  so switching back on returns to what you had.
#
#   neutral values a stage whose settings do nothing is skipped anyway --
#                  gaussian_blur at sigma 0, brightness at 0 gain 1,
#                  wavelet_denoise at luma 0 chroma 0. This costs nothing to
#                  use but means giving up the settings.
#
# The status line says how many stages were bypassed, so "did that actually
# skip?" is answerable rather than a matter of faith.

src = image("test")

src => params( gaussian_blur )()
    => params( brightness )()
    => params( wavelet_denoise )()
    => display( "stacked" )
